# Keep node scripts LF on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) too. Vite's SSR transform only recognises an
# LF hashbang; after `#!/usr/bin/env node\r\n` it hoists imports above the hashbang, so vitest fails
# to load scripts/verify-updater.test.mjs ("Invalid or unexpected token"). Unix also can't run a
# CRLF hashbang directly.
scripts/*.mjs text eol=lf
